  "body": "Process change: yes (this PR bumps `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 62 to 63 itself, the last PR to do so).\n\n**What changed.** The merging session is the single writer of `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`. Process PRs no longer edit it and say `Process change: yes` in the body; after a merge batch with a process PR the session runs the new `cargo xtask process-bump` (+1), merges a one-line PR and posts the #681 announcement. AGENTS.md, the PR-reviewer agent, and the review-prs, merge-ready and resolve-conflicts skills are updated. A fork still compares the same file, so nothing changes for it. Choices and dropped alternatives (merge-commit count, merge driver, Action) are in `docs/decisions/1153-process-version-single-writer.md`; no Actions trigger is added and no per-clone git config is needed.\n\n**Tests.** `xtask/src/process_bump_tests.rs` (bump +1, refusal of non-integer/overflow, file rewrite and argument refusal); quick gate green (xtask unit tests).\n\n**Not exercised.** The follow-up bump PR flow itself (first use is the merge of this PR); `merge-plan` still lists the file as MECHANICAL, kept for old branches.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\nFixes #1153\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
